  "worked_solution": "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $(0,2),$ the interval from $0$ to $2$ (not including $0$ nor $2$).\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $(0,2),$ the interval from $0$ to $2$ (not including $0$ nor $2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
